{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '148,169p;225,314p'\"","aggregated_output":"   148\t    @staticmethod\n   149\t    def estimate(request):\n   150\t        \"\"\"The shared reservation of one language-model attempt (WIRING-DESIGN.md §B): `llm_estimate`.\"\"\"\n   151\t        return llm_estimate(request)\n   152\t\n   153\t    def settle(self, reserved, actual, kind='llm', tokens=None):\n   154\t        \"\"\"Settle one attempt. A missing, non-finite, zero or negative charge settles at the whole reservation: an answered paid\n   155\t        request never costs nothing, and a failed attempt is charged its reservation. `kind` (llm, jev, embeddings) and the reported\n   156\t        `tokens` go to the attempt line only.\"\"\"\n   157\t        _LIVE.depth = max(0, getattr(_LIVE, 'depth', 0) - 1)\n   158\t        if not isinstance(actual, (int, float)) or isinstance(actual, bool) or not math.isfinite(actual) or actual <= 0:\n   159\t            actual = reserved\n   160\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   161\t            state['reserved'] = max(0.0, state['reserved'] - reserved)\n   162\t            state['spent'] += actual\n   163\t            if actual > reserved + 1e-12:\n   164\t                state['overrun'] = True\n   165\t                if not state.get('stopped'):\n   166\t                    state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, 'overrun'\n   167\t        self._note({'kind': kind, 'reserved': reserved, 'charged': actual, **({'tokens': tokens} if tokens is not None else {})})\n   168\t\n   169\t    def stop_if_a_launcher_is_gone(self):\n   225\t\n   226\t\n   227\tdef llm_estimate(request):\n   228\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   229\t    cap = request.get('max_completion_tokens', request.get('max_tokens'))\n   230\t    if isinstance(cap, bool) or not isinstance(cap, int) or cap <= 0:\n   231\t        raise model.TransportError('request without a positive output cap: refused by the budget')\n   232\t    tokens_in = 2 * len(json.dumps(request).encode('utf-8')) + 4096\n   233\t    return (tokens_in * price_in + cap * price_out) / 1e6\n   234\t\n   235\t\n   236\tdef whole(count):\n   237\t    return isinstance(count, int) and not isinstance(count, bool) and count >= 0\n   238\t\n   239\t\n   240\tdef llm_cost(response, request):\n   241\t    \"\"\"The answer's cost by `model.call`'s formula; None (settled at the reservation) unless the counts are whole, nonnegative numbers\n   242\t    with some input.\"\"\"\n   243\t    usage = response.get('usage') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   244\t    if not isinstance(usage, dict):\n   245\t        return None\n   246\t    tokens_in, tokens_out = usage.get('prompt_tokens'), usage.get('completion_tokens')\n   247\t    details = usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}\n   248\t    cached = (details.get('cached_tokens') or 0) if isinstance(details, dict) else None\n   249\t    if not (whole(tokens_in) and whole(tokens_out) and whole(cached)) or tokens_in == 0:\n   250\t        return None\n   251\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   252\t    cached = min(tokens_in, cached)\n   253\t    return (tokens_in - cached) / 1e6 * price_in + cached / 1e6 * price_in * model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + tokens_out / 1e6 * price_out\n   254\t\n   255\t\n   256\tdef jev_estimate(request):\n   257\t    price_in, _ = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   258\t    tokens_in = 2 * len(json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False).encode('utf-8')) + 4096\n   259\t    return jev.ATTEMPTS * tokens_in * price_in / 1e6\n   260\t\n   261\t\n   262\tclass BudgetTransport:\n   263\t    \"\"\"Called as production calls a transport: (provider, request) for a language model, (request,) for Jev.\"\"\"\n   264\t\n   265\t    def __init__(self, ledger, sleep=time.sleep):\n   266\t        self.ledger, self.sleep = ledger, sleep\n   267\t\n   268\t    def __call__(self, *args):\n   269\t        if len(args) == 1:\n   270\t            return self._jev(args[0])\n   271\t        provider, request = args\n   272\t        for attempt in range(3):\n   273\t            estimate = llm_estimate(request)\n   274\t            if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   275\t                raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   276\t            try:\n   277\t                response = model.openai_transport(provider, request, max_attempts=1)\n   278\t            except model.TransportError as error:\n   279\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   280\t                status = getattr(error, 'http_status', None)\n   281\t                if status in CLIENT_ERRORS or attempt == 2 or (status is not None and status != 429 and status < 500):\n   282\t                    raise\n   283\t                self.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n   284\t                continue\n   285\t            except Exception:\n   286\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   287\t                raise\n   288\t            cost = llm_cost(response, request)\n   289\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate if cost is None else cost)\n   290\t            return response\n   291\t        raise model.TransportError('no answer after three attempts')\n   292\t\n   293\t    def _jev(self, request):\n   294\t        estimate = jev_estimate(request)\n   295\t        if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   296\t            raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   297\t        try:\n   298\t            response = jev.transport(request)\n   299\t        except Exception:\n   300\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate, kind='jev')\n   301\t            raise\n   302\t        usage = response.get('usage') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   303\t        tokens = usage.get('input_tokens') if isinstance(usage, dict) else None\n   304\t        if isinstance(tokens, int) and not isinstance(tokens, bool) and tokens > 0:\n   305\t            # an unanswered attempt inside jev.transport was the same request, so each of the three is billed at most this input;\n   306\t            # the whole charge is settled, so a charge above the reservation sets the overrun flag\n   307\t            actual = jev.ATTEMPTS * tokens * model.PRICES[request['model']][0] / 1e6\n   308\t        else:\n   309\t            actual = estimate                       # usage missing, invalid, or zero for a nonempty request: the whole reservation\n   310\t        self.ledger.settle(estimate, actual, kind='jev', tokens=tokens if isinstance(tokens, int) else None)\n   311\t        return response\n   312\t\n   313\t\n   314\tdef main():\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py | sed -n '425,645p'\"","aggregated_output":"   425\t    proof = {'retired target rows': retired,\n   426\t             'an exact old v9 request goes to the transport': results['v9']['sent to the transport'],\n   427\t             'an exact old v14 request goes to the transport': results['v14']['sent to the transport'],\n   428\t             'an exact old v8 request is answered from the archive with its call id': results['v8']['call id kept'] and sent.count('v8') == 0,\n   429\t             'a retired (refused) answer is not returned again': len(sent) == before + 1}\n   430\t    print(json.dumps(proof, indent=1))\n   431\t    return all(v for k, v in proof.items() if isinstance(v, bool))\n   432\t\n   433\t\n   434\tCACHE_WRITE_SHARE = 1.25        # gpt-6-luna page and the prompt-caching guide, read 2026-11-21: cache writes $0.125 per 1M tokens, 1.25x input\n   435\tJEV_REQUEST_TOKENS = 64000       # TypeSafe's published default per-request limit (docs.typesafe.ai/models, context length), council R round 11\n   436\t\n   437\t\n   438\tdef settled_llm_cost(response, request):\n   439\t    \"\"\"The charge at the published rates: uncached input, cached input (0.1x) and cache writes (1.25x) are three disjoint parts of the\n   440\t    prompt tokens (the guide: \"input tokens use the uncached-input, cached-input, or cache-write rate\"), plus output; None when the\n   441\t    usage counts are not whole numbers with some input (the call then stays charged at its reservation).\"\"\"\n   442\t    usage = response.get('usage') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   443\t    if not isinstance(usage, dict):\n   444\t        return None\n   445\t    tokens_in, tokens_out = usage.get('prompt_tokens'), usage.get('completion_tokens')\n   446\t    details = usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}\n   447\t    cached = details.get('cached_tokens') or 0 if isinstance(details, dict) else None\n   448\t    written = details.get('cache_write_tokens') or 0 if isinstance(details, dict) else None\n   449\t    whole = lambda n: isinstance(n, int) and not isinstance(n, bool) and n >= 0\n   450\t    if not all(whole(n) for n in (tokens_in, tokens_out, cached, written)) or tokens_in == 0:\n   451\t        return None\n   452\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   453\t    cached = min(tokens_in, cached)\n   454\t    written = min(tokens_in - cached, written)\n   455\t    plain = tokens_in - cached - written\n   456\t    return (plain * price_in + cached * price_in * model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + written * price_in * CACHE_WRITE_SHARE + tokens_out * price_out) / 1e6\n   457\t\n   458\t\n   459\tdef budget_module():\n   460\t    \"\"\"The comparison runs' budget transport, with this harness's settlement (cache writes at their published rate) and Jev's\n   461\t    reservation at its published per-request limit for each of its attempts; the module is loaded for this harness alone.\"\"\"\n   462\t    import importlib.util\n   463\t    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('budget_replay_july', REPO / 'clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py')\n   464\t    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n   465\t    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n   466\t    module.llm_cost = settled_llm_cost\n   467\t    original_jev_estimate = module.jev_estimate\n   468\t    module.jev_estimate = lambda request: max(original_jev_estimate(request),\n   469\t                                              module.jev.ATTEMPTS * JEV_REQUEST_TOKENS * model.PRICES[request['model']][0] / 1e6)\n   470\t    return module\n   471\t\n   472\t\n   473\tdef bounds():\n   474\t    \"\"\"Every reservation the budget transport makes is an upper bound of what it then settles, checked on all of old-2's stored calls:\n   475\t    a Luna call settles its reported usage at published rates (`llm_cost`), never above `llm_estimate`; a Jev call settles\n   476\t    ATTEMPTS x reported input tokens, never above `jev_estimate`. With every settlement at or below its reservation, and a reservation\n   477\t    refused when spent + reserved + it would pass the ceiling, the ledger's spent never passes $0.15.\"\"\"\n   478\t    budget = budget_module()\n   479\t    archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2 / \"archive.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   480\t    worst = {'judge': 0.0, 'collision judge': 0.0, 'match (Jev)': 0.0}\n   481\t    counts = {'judge': 0, 'collision judge': 0, 'match (Jev)': 0}\n   482\t    for purpose, model_name, request_json, response_json, tokens_in in archive.execute(\n   483\t            \"select purpose, model, request_json, response_json, input_tokens from model_calls where purpose in ('judge', 'match')\"):\n   484\t        request = json.loads(request_json)\n   485\t        if model_name.startswith('jev'):\n   486\t            if not tokens_in:\n   487\t                continue\n   488\t            settled = budget.jev.ATTEMPTS * tokens_in * model.PRICES[model_name][0] / 1e6\n   489\t            ratio, key = settled / budget.jev_estimate(request), 'match (Jev)'\n   490\t        else:\n   491\t            settled = budget.llm_cost(json.loads(response_json), request)\n   492\t            if settled is None:\n   493\t                continue\n   494\t            ratio, key = settled / budget.llm_estimate(request), ('judge' if purpose == 'judge' else 'collision judge')\n   495\t        counts[key] += 1\n   496\t        worst[key] = max(worst[key], ratio)\n   497\t    result = {'calls checked': counts, 'largest settled / reserved': {k: round(v, 4) for k, v in worst.items()},\n   498\t              'every settlement within its reservation': all(v <= 1 for v in worst.values()) and all(counts.values())}\n   499\t    print(json.dumps(result, indent=1))\n   500\t    return result['every settlement within its reservation']\n   501\t\n   502\t\n   503\tdef price():\n   504\t    stored = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2 / \"archive.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   505\t    views = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2 / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   506\t    shas = [r[0] for r in views.execute(\"select request_sha256 from judgements where view_id in ('v9','v14') and publication_day between ? and ?\", WINDOW)]\n   507\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES['gpt-6-luna']\n   508\t    total, rows = 0.0, []\n   509\t    for sha in shas:\n   510\t        tokens_in, tokens_out = stored.execute('select input_tokens, output_tokens from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (sha,)).fetchone()\n   511\t        cost = tokens_in / 1e6 * price_in + tokens_out / 1e6 * price_out\n   512\t        rows.append((tokens_in, tokens_out, round(cost, 5)))\n   513\t        total += cost\n   514\t    v9 = [r for r, sha in zip(rows, shas) if views.execute(\"select view_id from judgements where request_sha256=?\", (sha,)).fetchone()[0] == 'v9']\n   515\t    extra_v9 = max(r[2] for r in v9) * 1.1               # a v9 call on 07-11 when v14 changes, with the dependency block (about 700 characters)\n   516\t    jev_in = model.PRICES['jev-1.14.0'][0]\n   517\t    jev_calls = 2 * 3 * 20000 * jev_in / 1e6             # two link jobs, Jev's three attempts, a generous 20,000 input tokens each\n   518\t    linked = total + extra_v9 + jev_calls\n   519\t    print(json.dumps({'stored v9/v14 judge calls in the window': rows, 'control sequence (uncached)': round(total, 4),\n   520\t                      'linked sequence, upper estimate (an extra v9 call, two link jobs)': round(linked, 4),\n   521\t                      'six sequences': round(3 * total + 3 * linked, 4), 'ceiling': CEILING}, indent=1))\n   522\t\n   523\t\n   524\tORDER = [('control-1', V118, False), ('linked-1', V119, True), ('control-2', V118, False), ('linked-2', V119, True),\n   525\t         ('control-3', V118, False), ('linked-3', V119, True)]       # alternated, so a ceiling stop falls on both arms alike\n   526\t\n   527\t\n   528\tdef send(prefix_ledger, out):\n   529\t    \"\"\"The paid comparison (run only after the council passed the $0 proof, D694 (c)): six sequences through the shared reservation ledger\n   530\t    of the comparison runs, one ceiling of $0.15; the ledger is read after each sequence, and a refused reservation or a stop makes the\n   531\t    comparison inconclusive and ends it.\"\"\"\n   532\t    budget = budget_module()\n   533\t    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)\n   534\t    ledger_path = out / 'ledger.json'\n   535\t    budget.SharedLedger.init(str(ledger_path), CEILING)\n   536\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(ledger_path))\n   537\t    remove_gate = budget.install_stop_gate(ledger)\n   538\t    transport = budget.BudgetTransport(ledger)\n   539\t    results, outcome = [], 'complete'\n   540\t    with open(out / 'send.log', 'a', encoding='utf-8') as log_file:\n   541\t        def log(*parts):\n   542\t            log_file.write(' '.join(str(p) for p in parts) + '\\n')\n   543\t            log_file.flush()\n   544\t        try:\n   545\t            for index, (name, cfg_path, linked) in enumerate(ORDER):\n   546\t                log(f'--- start {name}')\n   547\t                try:\n   548\t                    summary, _, _ = run_sequence(out, name, prefix_ledger, cfg_path, linked, transport, log)\n   549\t                except BaseException as error:              # a Python exception outside the sequence's own handling (an abrupt kill\n   550\t                    summary = {'name': name, 'started': True, 'stopped': f'{type(error).__name__}: {error}'[:400], 'comparable': False}\n   551\t                    outcome = f'stopped: {name} raised before its summary'          # leaves the start log and the ledger for inspection)\n   552\t                    results.append(summary)\n   553\t                    results.extend({'name': n, 'started': False} for n, _, _ in ORDER[index + 1:])\n   554\t                    raise\n   555\t                state = ledger.read()\n   556\t                summary['ledger_after'] = state\n   557\t                results.append(summary)\n   558\t                log(f'--- finish {name}: stopped={summary[\"stopped\"]!r} comparable={summary[\"comparable\"]} spent ${state[\"spent\"]:.4f} '\n   559\t                    f'reserved ${state[\"reserved\"]:.4f} refused {state[\"refused\"]}')\n   560\t                if state.get('stopped') or state.get('refused') or state.get('overrun'):\n   561\t                    outcome = 'inconclusive: the shared ledger stopped, refused or overran'\n   562\t                    results.extend({'name': n, 'started': False} for n, _, _ in ORDER[index + 1:])\n   563\t                    break\n   564\t                # a sequence that is not comparable stays stopped and is scored as such (the frozen rule counts comparable sequences);\n   565\t                # the other sequences are independent and go on while the shared ledger allows\n   566\t        finally:\n   567\t            remove_gate()\n   568\t            (out / 'send-summary.json').write_text(json.dumps({'outcome': outcome, 'ledger': ledger.read(), 'sequences': results}, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   569\t    print(outcome, ledger.read())\n   570\t\n   571\t\n   572\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   573\t    mode, scratch = sys.argv[1], Path(sys.argv[2])\n   574\t    scratch.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   575\t    if mode == 'prefix':\n   576\t        sys.exit(0 if prefix(scratch) else 1)\n   577\t    if mode == 'archive':\n   578\t        sys.exit(0 if archive_proof(scratch) else 1)\n   579\t    if mode == 'dry':\n   580\t        sys.exit(0 if dry(scratch, Path(sys.argv[3])) else 1)\n   581\t    if mode == 'price':\n   582\t        price()\n   583\t        sys.exit(0)\n   584\t    if mode == 'bounds':\n   585\t        sys.exit(0 if bounds() else 1)\n   586\t    if mode == 'send':\n   587\t        send(Path(sys.argv[3]), Path(sys.argv[4]))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A 34 '\"'^## D696'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/PROOF.md | sed -n '18,43p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A 34 '\"'^## D696'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/PROOF.md | sed -n '18,43p'\"","aggregated_output":"10467:## D696 · 2026-11-21 · Alex keeps the July test's $0.15 limit as a reservation stop priced from each request's size\n10468-\n10469-- **The question** (after council R round 11, `docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r11.md`): the budget\n10470-  transport reserves, before each model call, a worst case priced from the request's size (2 x its bytes + 4,096 input tokens, the full\n10471-  output cap) and refuses a call that would pass $0.15. Over 6,853 stored calls the charge never passed 31% of that reservation, but\n10472-  OpenAI publishes no bound tying a request's tokens to its size; its only published input bound (922,000 tokens) would reserve about\n10473-  $0.12 a call and make the test impossible under $0.15. Expected total about $0.09. Options: reserve from the request's size\n10474-  (recommended); or do not run.\n10475-- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-21): \"按请求长度预扣 (推荐)\".\n10476-- **Also fixed on council R's round-11 finding** (verified against the stored usage and the published pricing page, read 2026-11-21):\n10477-  gpt-6-luna bills cache writes at $0.125 per million tokens (1.25x input); every stored judge response reports `cache_write_tokens`.\n10478-  The July harness settles at the three published input rates (`july_test.settled_llm_cost`: the stored 07-10 Data Center call $0.002895,\n10479-  not $0.002662) and reserves each Jev request at TypeSafe's published 64K per-request limit for each of its three attempts. The\n10480-  product's own `model.call` cost records omit the cache-write premium too: a cost-reporting finding, recorded, not changed here.\n    18\t| the dry run (fake answers with a marker unique to sequence, question and attempt) | all checks true: in all four sequences each v9 and v14 request carries exactly its previous accepted answer (v9's first: old-2's 07-09 answer; v14's first: none); in the linked ones each v9 request shows exactly that day's accepted v14 comparison point and forecast; the link \"v9 reads v14\" (`first_is_bullish`, seq 148); a changed v14 on 07-11 queues v9, an unchanged one does not; controls judge v9 only on 07-10 and 07-12 and write no link; every target judgement a fresh call (\"comparable\") | `july_test.py dry`, `dry-run.log` |\n    19\t| the latch (two workers, deterministic) | a request admitted and held open; an unapproved request arriving meanwhile waits for it, is then refused and closes the latch; a later request is refused; only the first reached the inner transport (admission and the inner call run under one lock: a sequence's paid calls run one at a time) | `july_test.latch_race`, `dry-run.log` |\n    20\t| the stop paths, through replay | an unapproved judge request (v8's rows retired too): refused, v8 never forwarded, the latch stops the sequence, nothing judged after 07-10; a link request at another sequence: refused at seq 148, nothing forwarded; an out-of-pair link: stopped at inspection, no judge attempt, no item handed over after seq 148 | `dry-run.log` |\n    21\t| the request at the transport boundary | read by Claude: the linked v9 request of 07-10 (37,196 characters; 72 evidence lines; the dependency block, three themes, the previous conclusion, the closing sentence) | `linked-v9-0710-request.txt` |\n    22\t| the selection record on a failure | a Jev failure after an answered job: the jobs marked answered (with its call id), failed (its sha named), not asked; a write conflict: proposed then failed; a circle closed by a later insertion rolls back the whole write | `tests/test_links.py` |\n    23\t| reservations bound settlements | settled at the published rates including cache writes (1.25x; the stored 07-10 Data Center call $0.002895); over all of old-2's stored calls (1,620 judge, 70 collision judge, 5,163 Jev) the charge is at most 0.31 of the reservation; a reply without usage keeps its reservation; Jev reserved at the published 64K limit x 3 attempts ($0.0081). The Luna input bound is the request's size, kept by Alex's choice (D696) | `july_test.py bounds`, `settled_llm_cost` |\n    24\t| price | control sequence $0.0098 (the stored calls, uncached); linked sequence at most about $0.0185 (an extra v9 call, two link jobs); six sequences about $0.085; ceiling $0.15 | `july_test.py price` |\n    25\t| preflight | extraction 1,884 rows replayed, 69 statements dropped by the current checks (48 quote not in item, 21 merged; as in the stored run); matching 61 records judged, 0 refused, 1 skipped (request not in this archive); 4 judge answers the stored run itself refused and retried; enum names 46, none missing; 13 keyed views, no duplicate key. It does not replay the new link questions or judging-v8 (not in any archive): the dry run and the tests exercise them | `preflight.log` |\n    26\t| filing exposure | 105 reading answers after seq 148 link a statement to both v9 and v14 (total revenue's own Q1 figure and Q2 guidance among them); with `kind='reads'` none moves (re-filed by Codex in round 9: 105 of 105 keep both links) | `filing-exposure.md`, test 5 |\n    27\t| the reading rule | frozen: `reading-rule.md` (sha256 below) | |\n    28\t\n    29\tWritten, not run: `july_test.py send <scratch> <prefix ledger> <out>`: six sequences alternated (control-1, linked-1, ... under\n    30\tpoc-v118 and poc-v119) through `run_sequence` with `BudgetTransport` over a new `SharedLedger` (ceiling $0.15) and `install_stop_gate`.\n    31\tEach sequence's start and finish are logged; after each, the shared ledger is read (stopped, refused or overrun: inconclusive) and the\n    32\tsequence's own result (a stop or a target judgement that was not fresh: not comparable). Only the shared ledger ends the send (the\n    33\tsequences not started are listed); a sequence that is not comparable stays stopped, is scored as not comparable, and the other\n    34\tindependent sequences go on. The summary is written on any normal exit or Python exception; an abrupt kill leaves the start log and the\n    35\tledger. It runs only after the council passes this proof. Not done: the PRD 06 text for the\n    36\tnew matcher outcome (it changes with the decision that makes a version the product).\n    37\treading-rule.md sha256: cc876b60b8eef25b7675f6d078147d2e569ec97d1b1bfa969f9ec8060d596680\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
