{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run; rg -n 'retries|unknown|Jev|D696' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/WIRING-DESIGN.md | head -36\"","aggregated_output":"ledgers\nnew-1\nnew-1.launcher.log\nnew-1.pid\nnew-2\nnew-2.launcher.log\nnew-2.pid\nnew-3\nnew-3.launcher.log\nnew-3.pid\nold-1\nold-1.launcher.log\nold-1.pid\nold-2\nold-2.launcher.log\nold-2.pid\nold-3\nold-3.launcher.log\nold-3.pid\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/WIRING-DESIGN.md:31:| embeddings (`hivemind.search.openai_embeddings`, called by `step2/run_forward.py`) | the budgeted Step 2 runner replaces the module attribute before calling `run_forward.main`; the replacement reserves, then calls the original | three attempts (the helper retries inside) × (2 × request bytes + 4,096) tokens at the embedding rate | three times the reported total tokens; zero or missing: the reservation |\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/WIRING-DESIGN.md:32:| Jev (Step 2 and production) | as `budget_replay.py` (`jev.transport` patched in Step 2's runner; the transport argument in production) | three attempts × the input bound | three times the reported input; zero or missing: the reservation |\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/WIRING-DESIGN.md:58:- **Jev:** the budgeted Step 2 runner captures the original `jev.transport` before replacing it, and the wrapper calls the captured\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/WIRING-DESIGN.md:93:5. **The ledger under stress:** concurrent sends, retries inside a component, missing usage, an overrun, a held reservation after a\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/WIRING-DESIGN.md:102:own retries); otherwise the run stops. The ladder step and the judge have no outer redo (the judge keeps its own inside `run_stage_b.py`).\nclean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/WIRING-DESIGN.md:111:| Step 2 draw | stamped | reported | the helper's retries, then the draw stops: one reasoned redo (D449) | the run stops | recorded; the run stops (D449) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:23:   judgement on 07-11). The linked dry sequences must write \"v9 reads v14\" at seq 148 (fixed Jev answers) and show the judging-v8 block\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:44:wrapper, built by the serial item runner for one item, passes only Jev requests whose questions are all link questions (the READS and\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:55:Luna call reserves its worst case per attempt and settles at its reported usage; a Jev call reserves its whole internal retry bundle\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:58:or judging failure; an overrun or an unknown charge is reported from the ledger.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c 'import sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\").resolve()\nby_request={}\nfor n in (\\\"old-1\\\",\\\"old-2\\\",\\\"old-3\\\",\\\"new-1\\\",\\\"new-2\\\",\\\"new-3\\\"):\n    for a in (root/n).glob(\\\"**/archive.sqlite\\\"):\n        db=sqlite3.connect(a.as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\n        for request,tokens in db.execute(\\\"select request_sha256,input_tokens from model_calls where model=\\\\x27jev-1.14.0\\\\x27 and input_tokens > 0\\\"):\n            by_request.setdefault(request.split(\\\":\\\")[0],[]).append(tokens)\nrepeated=[v for v in by_request.values() if len(v)>1]\nnonconstant=[v for v in repeated if len(set(v))>1]\nprint(\\\"identical Jev request groups\\\",len(repeated),\\\"with different reported input\\\",len(nonconstant),\\\"examples\\\",nonconstant[:3])'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c 'import importlib.util,json,sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\nspec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\\\"july_review\\\",Path(\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py\\\"))\nh=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nspec.loader.exec_module(h)\nh.bounds()\nb=h.budget_module()\nview=sqlite3.connect((h.OLD2/\\\"views.sqlite\\\").as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\ndb=sqlite3.connect((h.OLD2/\\\"archive.sqlite\\\").as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\nsha,=view.execute(\\\"select request_sha256 from judgements where view_id=\\\\x27v9\\\\x27 and publication_day=\\\\x272026-07-10\\\\x27\\\").fetchone()\nreq,resp=map(json.loads,db.execute(\\\"select request_json,response_json from model_calls where request_sha256=?\\\",(sha,)).fetchone())\nprint(\\\"v9 July 10\\\",resp[\\\"usage\\\"],\\\"charged\\\",b.llm_cost(resp,req),\\\"est\\\",b.llm_estimate(req),\\\"missing\\\",b.llm_cost({},req))\nreq=json.loads(db.execute(\\\"select request_json from model_calls where model=\\\\x27jev-1.14.0\\\\x27 limit 1\\\").fetchone()[0])\nprint(\\\"Jev reservation\\\",b.jev_estimate(req))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
