{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"The July send is ready under D696. Alex approved the **$0.15 request-size reservation stop**, so the unpublished Luna input bound no longer blocks this test. [D696](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10467)\n\n- **Luna settlement checks out.** The stored July 10 Data Center call had 3 ordinary input tokens, 1,167 cache reads, 9,305 cache writes, and 3,440 output tokens. At the published rates, the harness settles it at **$0.002895095**. I also verified that a reply without usage charges the full reservation. [Settlement code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:438) · [Luna pricing](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6-luna#pricing)\n- **Jev reservation checks out.** Three attempts at the published 64,000-token limit and $0.042 per million input tokens give a minimum reservation of **$0.008064**. With no usable usage in the final reply, the transport charges the full reservation. I reran the census across 6,853 stored calls and reproduced **31.2%** as the largest settlement relative to its reservation. [Harness budget setup](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/july_test.py:459) · [TypeSafe model limits and pricing](https://docs.typesafe.ai/models)\n\n**Nonblocking:** Rename the proof row “reservations bound settlements” to “historical settlements stayed within reservations.” That describes the census and keeps the report aligned with Alex’s decision. The harness uses the corrected settlement through its own budget module. The product cost-record issue is separately recorded in D696. [Proof table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/PROOF.md:23)\n\n**READY TO SEND**"}}
